SUMMARY:Death on a Dime （Mid-Week Edition）
DESCRIPTION:The dime hit the floor with a metallic ∗ting∗ that cut thro
 ugh the silence. Everyone in the diner looked down. Everyone except the man
  in the gray coat. He kept stirring his coffee. The Defective noticed three
  things at once: the dead bartender slumped on the pool table‚ the waitre
 ss backing away in the closet‚ and the thin line of blood running beneath
  the sugar dispenser beside the mans elbow. Dont move‚ they said. The mur
 der smiled faintly. You dont have proof. The detective bent down and picked
  up the dime. Fresh blood coated Roosevelts face. The room went still. The 
 killers smile vanished. Then the lights went out. A gunshot cracked through
  the darkness. Someone screamed. And the detective had exactly two choices:
  Catch the murderer red-handed or run for there life.
LOCATION:VRChat
